{"schema":"main812-bytecode-candidate-1","observed_at_utc":"2026-11-10T10:17:00Z","pull":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/pulls/812","id":5239560217,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQpeC2s8AAAABOE1YGQ","html_url":"https://github.com/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/pull/812","diff_url":"https://github.com/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/pull/812.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/pull/812.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/issues/812","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/pulls/812/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/pulls/812/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/issues/812/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/statuses/1d7dab56310c8912ade8e94275f1e6ac0c4158b7","number":812,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Prevent custody fault tests from writing bytecode","user":{"login":"d6g8k5htny-coder","id":249851642,"node_id":"U_kgDODuRu-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249851642?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder","html_url":"https://github.com/d6g8k5htny-coder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d6g8k5htny-coder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The custody OSError tests start a child Python interpreter without `-B`. When the outer suite runs with `-B` and `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE` is unset, the child can leave `tools/__pycache__/periodic_pilot_custody.*.pyc` in the checkout. That conflicts with the clean-source guard exercised by Main #809.\n\nAdd `-B` to that child invocation and an isolated behavioral regression that runs the real fault path with the environment variable absent. The two existing OSError checks remain intact. Removing the added flag makes the new regression fail in both modes.\n\nOn the #809 tested tree, a separate instrumented hosted diagnostic observed `tools/__pycache__/periodic_pilot_custody.cpython-311.pyc` immediately before and after the same `SOURCE_MISMATCH` setup error. Its context differs from the original failing navigation run, which did not record the path; this is not a retroactive identification of the original file. The original diagnostic artifact, logs, exact source blobs, red controls and local reproductions are preserved at [evidence commit 8c3d8a55](https://github.com/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/blob/8c3d8a55a947138e23c741f42654bb1c137c4080/cbz/evidence/main809-navigation-20261110/observer/observer-verified-summary.json).\n\nLocal focused checks: 3 tests per mode on CPython 3.12.14 and 3.13.5, no skips. The original invocation with the new regression failed once in each mode as expected. Hosted checks remain pending; no full G5, CBZ-0 or scientific conclusion is claimed. This draft targets the active #809 branch and does not alter its ref.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-10T10:16:12Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T10:16:12Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"89c5601cd4c99990d02daf1efdfe2d030dad9c00","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"d6g8k5ht